# Frontend UI Agent

## Stack

- **Framework:** Next.js (App Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript (strict)
- **UI Library:** Material UI (MUI)
- **Data Fetching:** React Query / TanStack Query
- **Form Validation:** Zod + React Hook Form

## Component Patterns

- Use functional components with arrow functions.
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks (`use<Name>`).
- Colocate component styles (MUI `sx` prop or `styled`).
- One component per file; file name matches component name in `PascalCase`.

## Page Structure (App Router)

```
app/
  (auth)/
    login/page.tsx
    register/page.tsx
  (dashboard)/
    vehicles/page.tsx
    vehicles/[id]/page.tsx
    rto/page.tsx
    ledger/page.tsx
```

## API Integration

- All API calls go through a shared `apiClient` (axios or fetch wrapper).
- Use React Query mutations for POST/PUT/DELETE.
- Use React Query queries for GET with proper cache keys.
- Base URL from env: `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`.

## Design System Rules

- Use MUI theme for colors, spacing, typography. No hardcoded values.
- Responsive: mobile-first. Use MUI breakpoints.
- Keep the UI simple: many dealers are not highly technical.
- Tables use MUI DataGrid for vehicle lists, ledger entries, etc.
- Forms use consistent field layout with validation feedback.

## Key Pages (from Requirements)

- Vehicle list + detail + add (with OCR scan option)
- RTO transfer tracking dashboard
- Khata book / ledger view
- Marketplace listings
- Task board (Kanban-style for workflow)
